    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "VANILLA: (GER. Vanilje. DU. Ba- nille. DA. Vaniller. SW. Baniller. FR. Vanille. IR. Vainiglia. SP. Vainilla, Vainica. PORT. Vainilha, Baonelha. LAT. Vanilla.) There are 124 species of the vanilla plant, one of which produces this fruit, which is used in making chocolate. It is a native of Mexico, and also of some parts of the East Indies. It is a parasitic p..."@en ;
